  "attack_surface": "To close bi-tight for all p\u22655, prove ONE of:\n  (A) mult(\u03bb\u2082(P\u2299P))\u2265d and \u2211M\u00b2\u22644d\u00b2(d+4)  [gap via two-moment];\n  (B) \u03bb_max(FFT|1\u22a5)\u22648N  [16N];\n  (C) \u03bb_max(FFT|1\u22a5)\u2264N(3+H)  [H];\n  (D) max|m4|\u2264(p\u22122)/(2p\u00b2) on |\u03ba|=1  [m4 path, Prop 15.66].\nNew structure: P\u2299P kills range(P) (central symmetry). At p=5, (A) holds with certified mult=d and exact Q. Need mult\u2265d for general p, and control of \u2211M\u00b2 (or \u2211\u03ba\u00b2).",
  "verdict": "Prop 15.94 proves P\u2299P annihilates range(P) by vanishing third moments (central symmetry), and records the gap criterion mult(\u03bb\u2082)\u2265d + \u2211M\u00b2\u22644d\u00b2(d+4). Certified at p=5: mult=d and criterion holds for gap (not for 16N). General mult\u2265d and \u2211M\u00b2 bound OPEN. 16N/H OPEN. lim \u03b1_n OPEN.",
  "settlement_note": "Next: prove mult(\u03bb\u2082(P\u2299P))\u2265d for all primes p\u22655 (representation / explicit d-dimensional test space), and \u2211M_ijkl\u00b2\u22644d\u00b2(d+4). Then gap\u21d2bi-tight empty. Or prove \u03bb_max(FFT|1\u22a5)\u22648N. Deep ND remains.",
  "proved": true
